        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Cr(NO3)3·9H2O (1 mmol, 0.400 g) and Ln(NO3)3·5H2O (Ln = Dy for 1; 0.5 mmol, 0.22 g) were dissolved in 20 mL of acetonitrile, followed by addition of benzoic acid (1 mmol, 0.122 g) and triethylamine (4 mmol, 0.55 mL). The solution was stirred for 4 h at ambient temperature. The solvent was removed to form a gel, which was redissolved in 20 mL of iPrOH. Purple single crystals suitable for X-ray analysis formed after a week of evaporation (approx. 45% crystalline yield).",
