      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Pentanuclear {Cr2Dy3} SMM. Room-temperature χMT = 45.67 cm3 K mol−1 (calc. 46.26). χMT remains nearly constant to 100.2 K, falls to 20.6 cm3 K mol−1 at 40.5 K, then rises to 101.5 cm3 K mol−1 at 1.8 K, indicating ferromagnetic Cr–Dy coupling. Magnetization at 2–10 K reaches 16.28 μB (2 T) and 18.9 μB (7 T). Zero-field ac susceptibility (1–900 Hz, 2–2.8 K) shows frequency-dependent χ′/χ″ peaks. Arrhenius fit (Orbach + Raman) gives Ueff = 30.9 K (21.4 cm−1), τ0 = 4.09×10−10 s, n = 6.3, C = 19.85 s−1 K−6.3. Computed exchanges: JDy–Dy = +0.012 cm−1, JCr–Dy = +1.20 cm−1, JCr–Cr = −0.95 cm−1.",
