        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Isostructural {Cr2Gd3} analogue used to quantify isotropic exchanges. Room-temperature χMT = 27.11 cm3 K mol−1 (calc. 27.38). χMT nearly constant to 102.0 K, then rises to 59.3 cm3 K mol−1 at 4.4 K. Magnetization reaches 27.27 μB (2 T) and 28.02 μB (7 T); saturation ~27 μB at 2 K supports S = 27/2 from dominant ferromagnetic coupling. PHI fit: JGd–Gd = +0.008 cm−1, JCr–Gd = +0.27 cm−1, JCr–Cr = −0.007 cm−1. DFT: J1 = +0.015, J2 = +1.38, J3 = −0.558 cm−1. No ac SMM parameters reported for 2.",
